drm/msm/dpu: round the compressed DSI INTF width up

With DSC the DPU INTF active width is the number of pixel clocks needed
to send one compressed line. 6.12 truncates it:

  width = width * bpp / (bpc * 3)

The DSI host programs ACTIVE_H with DIV_ROUND_UP(bytes_per_line, 3), and
the downstream SDE driver uses pclk_per_line = DIV_ROUND_UP(bytes, 3) for
both DSI and INTF. TB371FC (2 slices of 736 px per DSI, 8 bpp, 8 bpc):
1472 bytes per line -> DSI 491 pclk, DPU 490 pclk. The 1-pclk mismatch
gives a continuous DSI FIFO error (dsi_err_worker status=4) after kickoff.

Round up so INTF and DSI agree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -128,12 +128,10 @@ static void drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params(
 	if (phys_enc->hw_intf->cap->type != INTF_DP && timing->compression_en) {
 		struct drm_dsc_config *dsc =
 		       dpu_encoder_get_dsc_config(phys_enc->parent);
-		/*
-		 * TODO: replace drm_dsc_get_bpp_int with logic to handle
-		 * fractional part if there is fraction
-		 */
-		timing->width = timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) /
-				(dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
+		/* Match DSI ACTIVE_H and downstream pclk_per_line: round up. */
+		timing->width = DIV_ROUND_UP(timing->width *
+					     drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc),
+					     dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
 		timing->xres = timing->width;
 	}
 }
